# Section 4, "Reflective Non-Sequential Surfaces": NEW entering the two NSReflector faces Face1 and Face2
# of the corner-cube discussion (Figure 25: a roof of two flat faces whose order of strike depends on the
# ray).  The answers to the two face dialogs are 3.2's (vertex and rotation point 0,0,0, principal axes
# -.7071,0,-.7071 and .7071,0,-.7071, zElt 1d22, Geometric, index 1d0).  3.2 printed only the two face
# dialogs; NEW needs a complete deck, so the source (rays along +z toward the roof, the chief ray offset
# 1d-5 off the ridge as in examples/CornerCube.in), the sequential Reference before the faces and the
# FocalPlane after them are entered as setup and not printed.  Differences from 3.2's dialog: the
# current dialog adds the glass-type prompt (answered with its default, FixedIndex), prints the element
# back and asks "Is this correct?" (default YES); the element and surface type lists are longer;
# psiElt is stored normalized (0.70711, not .7071).  The roof returns every ray to the reference plane
# with the same path: the OPD at the focal plane is at the round-off floor.
cd $TMP
new
Roof
0,0,1
1d-5,1d-5,-10
1d22
1
0
none
1d-6
1
Circular
1
11
1,0,0
0,1,0
4
RefSrf
Reference
Flat
0,0,-3.5
0,0,-3.5
0,0,1


0
Geometric


